IMPORT prelude

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014 (Singapore) -- whether I must register, whether the name I want is open to me, who must
-- appoint an authorised representative, the notices I must lodge and by when, what I can appeal, restoration, and what I can be
-- fined.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who carries on, or proposes to carry on, business in Singapore -- as an individual proprietor (sole
-- proprietor) or as a partner of a firm.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2(1) ("business", "full name", "individual proprietor", "firm"), s 2(2); s 4(1)(a) to (d), (p), (q), 4(2),
-- 4(3); s 5; s 6(3) ("appropriate person"); ss 8(7), 9, 10(1); s 11(1) to (4), (7), (9), (11), (12), (14); s 12(4); s 13(2), (3);
-- s 14(4); s 16(4), (5); s 17(1) to (3), (9); ss 19, 20(1) to (3); s 22(1), (3), (4); s 24(1), (2); ss 34(1), 35, 36, 37(1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 9 June 2025 ("Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BNRA2014-2026-10-01.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 2(3) (when a foreign company is not carrying on business in Singapore) and s 4(1)(e) to (o) (statutory bodies,
-- societies, companies, LLPs, limited partnerships and the like): not the seat; the Registrar's administration (s 3), rectification
-- (ss 25 to 27), copies, the electronic system, inspection and information powers (ss 28 to 33), records (s 38), enforcement orders
-- (s 39), bodies corporate (s 40), service (s 42), regulations (s 43) and the transitional provisions (s 45). No regulations under
-- s 43 were deposited, so what they would prescribe (who else is exempt, which professions lose the s 4(1)(c) exemption, which
-- offences are compoundable) is asked as a fact. The particulars of an application (s 6(1)(b)) are not checked.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE AS ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Business Names Registration Act 2014 -- registration`

§§ `s 2 -- my business, and my full name`

-- s 2(1): "business" includes every form of trade, commerce and profession, and any other activity, "that is carried on for the
-- purposes of gain, but does not include any office, employment or occupation".
-- "full name" means (a) for an individual registered under the National Registration Act 1965, "the name as it appears in the
-- latest identity card"; (b) otherwise the name in the latest passport "or such other similar evidence of identification".
-- "individual proprietor" means an individual carrying on business as a sole proprietor.
-- "firm" means an unincorporated body of 2 or more individuals (or individuals and corporations, or corporations) in partnership
-- "with a view to carrying on business for profit".
-- s 2(2): "A person who has a place of business in Singapore is to be treated as carrying on business in Singapore".

DECLARE `How I carry on business` IS ONE OF
    `as an individual proprietor`   -- a sole proprietor
    `as a partner of a firm`        -- a partnership, s 2(1) "firm"

DECLARE `My business` HAS
    `how I carry it on`                                       IS A `How I carry on business`
    `it is carried on for gain`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an office or employment or occupation`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a place of business in Singapore`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I otherwise carry on business in Singapore`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the business name`                                       IS A STRING
    -- the name I trade under
    `my full name`                                            IS A STRING
    -- s 2(1): the name on my latest NRIC, or on my latest passport if I am not registered under the National Registration Act
    `every partner is an individual`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the firm trades under only the full names of all its partners` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is solely a profession only registered qualified people may exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulations take my profession out of the exemption`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(2); no regulations were deposited, so this is asked
    `a nominee or trustee carries it on for me and gave the section 7 particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a First Schedule business I have carried on since before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(1)(q): First Schedule to the Business Registration Act (Cap. 32, 2004 Rev Ed), borrowed and asked
    `regulations exempt me`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(1)(p); no regulations were deposited, so this is asked

GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I carrying on a business` IF
        `my business`'s `it is carried on for gain`
    AND NOT `my business`'s `it is an office or employment or occupation`

-- s 2(2) treats a place of business as enough; it does not say it is the only way, so "otherwise" is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I carrying on business in Singapore` IF
        `Am I carrying on a business` `my business`
    AND (   `my business`'s `I have a place of business in Singapore`
         OR `my business`'s `I otherwise carry on business in Singapore`)

§§ `ss 4 and 5 -- must I register?`

-- s 5(1): "before a person carries on business in Singapore, the person and the person's business name must be registered."
-- s 5(2): a separate registration for each business name.
-- s 4(1): "The following persons are not required to be registered": (a) "any individual proprietor carrying on business under
-- only the individual proprietor's full name"; (b) "any firm of 2 or more individuals carrying on business under only the full
-- names of all the individuals"; (c) subject to (2), an individual or firm of individuals carrying on business "consisting solely of
-- the exercise of any profession" open only to those with prescribed qualifications whose names are registered or recorded;
-- (d) a person for whom another carries on business wholly or mainly as nominee or trustee, "if B has provided the particulars
-- required under section 7(1)"; (p) persons exempted by regulations; (q) an individual proprietor carrying on a First Schedule
-- business immediately before 3 January 2016 "who is alive and continues to carry on the same business".
-- s 4(3): a person not required to be registered, "other than a person who is specified in any of the provisions of subsection
-- (1)(e) to (o), may choose to be registered."

GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my firm one of individuals only` IF
    CONSIDER `my business`'s `how I carry it on`
    WHEN `as a partner of a firm` THEN `my business`'s `every partner is an individual`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from registering` IF
        -- (a) a sole proprietor trading under nothing but the full name
        (    `my business`'s `how I carry it on` EQUALS `as an individual proprietor`
         AND `my business`'s `the business name` EQUALS `my business`'s `my full name`)
        -- (b) a firm of individuals trading under nothing but all their full names
    OR  (    `Is my firm one of individuals only` `my business`
         AND `my business`'s `the firm trades under only the full names of all its partners`)
        -- (c) a regulated profession, unless regulations under s 43 take it out (s 4(2))
    OR  (    (   `my business`'s `how I carry it on` EQUALS `as an individual proprietor`
              OR `Is my firm one of individuals only` `my business`)
         AND `my business`'s `it is solely a profession only registered qualified people may exercise`
         AND NOT `my business`'s `regulations take my profession out of the exemption`)
        -- (d) a nominee or trustee carries it on for me
    OR  `my business`'s `a nominee or trustee carries it on for me and gave the section 7 particulars`
        -- (p) exempted by regulations
    OR  `my business`'s `regulations exempt me`
        -- (q) an old First Schedule business, carried on by the same living sole proprietor
    OR  (    `my business`'s `how I carry it on` EQUALS `as an individual proprietor`
         AND `my business`'s `it is a First Schedule business I have carried on since before 3 January 2016`)

GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I register` IF
        `Am I carrying on business in Singapore` `my business`
    AND NOT `Am I exempt from registering` `my business`

-- s 4(3): every exemption open to the individual is outside (e) to (o), so an exempt individual may always choose to register.
GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I choose to register although I need not` IF
        `Am I carrying on business in Singapore` `my business`
    AND `Am I exempt from registering` `my business`

§§ `s 6(3) -- who may lodge my application`

-- s 6(1)(a): an application "is to be lodged with the Registrar by an appropriate person". s 6(3) "appropriate person": (a) for
-- an individual proprietor, "that individual"; (e) for a firm, "an individual who is ... a partner of the firm" (or the appropriate
-- person of a corporate partner); (f) "a registered corporate service provider who is authorised by, and is acting for, the person
-- seeking to be registered".

DECLARE `Who lodges` IS ONE OF
    `I lodge it myself`
    `another partner of my firm`
    `a registered corporate service provider authorised by and acting for me`
    `a friend or employee of mine`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I carry on business`, `who` IS A `Who lodges`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person lodge my application` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `I lodge it myself` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered corporate service provider authorised by and acting for me` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another partner of my firm` THEN `how` EQUALS `as a partner of a firm`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 17 -- is a name identical to an earlier one open to me?`

-- s 17(1): "Except with the Minister's consent or as provided in subsection (3)", the Registrar "must refuse" a name that "is
-- identical to any other registered business name, or the name of any corporation or limited partnership".
-- s 17(2): except with the Minister's consent, the Registrar must refuse a name identical to: (a) a business name cancelled under
-- this Act or ceased under s 22, "unless a period of at least one year has passed"; (b) a dissolved company -- (i) after winding up,
-- at least 2 years; (ii) after being struck off, at least 6 years; (c) a foreign company whose dissolution was notified, at least 2
-- years; (d) a dissolved LLP -- (i) after winding up, 2 years; (ii) after being struck off, 6 years; (e) a limited partnership --
-- (i) cancelled, one year; (ii) notified as dissolved, one year.
-- s 17(3): "Despite subsection (1), the Registrar MAY register" a name identical to (a)(i) a registered foreign company that ceased
-- business in Singapore, after at least 3 months; (a)(ii) one whose name was struck off, after at least 6 years; (b) a limited
-- partnership that ceased business in Singapore, after at least one year.

DECLARE `Earlier holder of the identical name` IS ONE OF
    `a live registered business name or corporation or limited partnership`
    `a business name cancelled or ceased under this Act`
    `a company dissolved after winding up`
    `a company dissolved after being struck off`
    `a foreign company whose dissolution was notified`
    `a limited liability partnership dissolved after winding up`
    `a limited liability partnership dissolved after being struck off`
    `a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled`
    `a limited partnership notified as dissolved`
    `a registered foreign company that ceased business in Singapore`
    `a registered foreign company whose name was struck off`
    `a limited partnership that ceased business in Singapore`

-- The waiting periods of s 17(2) and (3), as a table, in months (one year = 12). NOTHING: the bar never runs out.
GIVEN `holder` IS AN `Earlier holder of the identical name`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the months that must pass before the name can be taken` IS
    CONSIDER `holder`
    WHEN `a live registered business name or corporation or limited partnership` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a business name cancelled or ceased under this Act`                    THEN JUST 12
    WHEN `a company dissolved after winding up`                                  THEN JUST 24
    WHEN `a company dissolved after being struck off`                            THEN JUST 72
    WHEN `a foreign company whose dissolution was notified`                      THEN JUST 24
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership dissolved after winding up`            THEN JUST 24
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership dissolved after being struck off`      THEN JUST 72
    WHEN `a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled`                THEN JUST 12
    WHEN `a limited partnership notified as dissolved`                           THEN JUST 12
    WHEN `a registered foreign company that ceased business in Singapore`        THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `a registered foreign company whose name was struck off`                THEN JUST 72
    WHEN `a limited partnership that ceased business in Singapore`               THEN JUST 12

-- s 17(3) says "may": once its period has run the Registrar has a choice, not a duty.
GIVEN `holder` IS AN `Earlier holder of the identical name`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the name open only at the Registrar's choice` IF
    CONSIDER `holder`
    WHEN `a registered foreign company that ceased business in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered foreign company whose name was struck off`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership that ceased business in Singapore`        THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Name position` IS ONE OF
    `barred to me`
    `open to me as far as this rule goes`
    `open to me only if the Registrar chooses to register it`

-- "at least N years has passed": read as N x 12 whole months having passed (an inference; the day count is not modelled).
GIVEN `holder` IS AN `Earlier holder of the identical name`
      `months passed` IS A NUMBER
      -- whole months since the cancellation, cessation, dissolution or striking off
      `the Minister consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Name position`
DECIDE `Can I take a name identical to an earlier one` IS
    IF `the Minister consents`
    THEN `open to me as far as this rule goes`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the months that must pass before the name can be taken` `holder`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `barred to me`
         WHEN JUST `required` THEN
             IF `months passed` LESS THAN `required`
             THEN `barred to me`
             ELSE IF `is the name open only at the Registrar's choice` `holder`
                  THEN `open to me only if the Registrar chooses to register it`
                  ELSE `open to me as far as this rule goes`

§§ `ss 9 and 17(1) -- must my application be refused?`

-- s 9: "Despite any provision in this Act or any other written law", the Registrar "must refuse" where "the Registrar is satisfied
-- that" (a) the business is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good
-- order; (b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest; (c) a foreign company not registered (not the seat).
-- s 13(1): a certificate of the Minister for internal security on (b) is "conclusive evidence".
-- s 17(1): except with the Minister's consent, must refuse a name that "in the Registrar's opinion" (a) "is undesirable"; (b)
-- identical (above); (c) identical to a reserved name; (d) of a kind the Minister has directed by Gazette notification not be
-- accepted.
-- Every judgment here is someone else's; each is asked as a fact ("if the Registrar is satisfied that ...").

DECLARE `What others have decided about my application` HAS
    `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied or the Minister certifies it is against national security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar thinks the name undesirable`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name is identical to a reserved name`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name is of a kind the Minister has directed not be accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister consents to the name`                         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `decided` IS A `What others have decided about my application`
      `name position` IS A `Name position`
      -- from `Can I take a name identical to an earlier one`, or `open to me as far as this rule goes` if no identical name
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my application be refused` IF
        -- s 9: no consent cures these
        `decided`'s `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose`
    OR  `decided`'s `the Registrar is satisfied or the Minister certifies it is against national security`
        -- s 17(1)(a), (c), (d): the Minister's consent cures these
    OR  (    NOT `decided`'s `the Minister consents to the name`
         AND (   `decided`'s `the Registrar thinks the name undesirable`
              OR `decided`'s `the name is identical to a reserved name`
              OR `decided`'s `the name is of a kind the Minister has directed not be accepted`))
        -- s 17(1)(b), (2): an identical name still barred
    OR  `name position` EQUALS `barred to me`

-- s 10(1): registration "does not confer on the person any property in the registered business name".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does registration make the name my property` IF FALSE

§§ `s 16(4) -- how long my name stays reserved`

-- s 16(4): the name is reserved from receipt of the application until (a) if approved, "60 days after the date on which the
-- Registrar notifies the applicant that the application has been approved, or such further period of 60 days as the Registrar
-- may, on application made in good faith, extend"; (b) if refused, the date the refusal is notified.
-- The text does not cap the number of extensions; each is taken to add 60 days (an inference).

GIVEN `approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `extensions granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after notice of the decision does my reservation last` IS
    IF `approved`
    THEN 60 PLUS 60 TIMES `extensions granted`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 8(7), 12(4), 13, 16(5), 17(9) -- what I can appeal, and how long I have`

-- s 8(7): a person aggrieved by a refusal to register or to renew "may, within 30 days after the date the person is notified of
-- that refusal, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final". s 13(2): not where the refusal is under s 9(b) "on the basis of a
-- certificate".
-- s 12(4): cancellation under s 12(1) or (2): "within 30 days ... or such further period as the Minister may allow"; s 13(3): not
-- where the cancellation is under s 12(1)(a)(ii) on a certificate.
-- s 16(5): refusal to reserve, or to extend a reservation: 30 days. s 17(9): a direction to change the name: 30 days.
-- No appeal is given in ss 14, 17(8) or 23 against cancellation for failure to renew, for not obeying a direction, or for not
-- carrying on business.

DECLARE `Decision against me` IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to register me`
    `a refusal to renew my registration`
    `a cancellation of my registration under section 12`
    `a refusal to reserve a name`
    `a refusal to extend my reservation`
    `a direction to change my business name`
    `a cancellation for failure to renew`
    `a cancellation for not obeying a direction to change my name`
    `a cancellation because I was not carrying on business`

GIVEN `decision` IS A `Decision against me`
      `it rests on an internal security certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `further days the Minister allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to appeal to the Minister` IS
    CONSIDER `decision`
    WHEN `a refusal to register me` THEN
        IF `it rests on an internal security certificate` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST 30
    WHEN `a refusal to renew my registration` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a cancellation of my registration under section 12` THEN
        IF `it rests on an internal security certificate` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (30 PLUS `further days the Minister allows`)
    WHEN `a refusal to reserve a name` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a refusal to extend my reservation` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a direction to change my business name` THEN JUST 30
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 11 -- authorised representative`

-- s 11(1): where "an individual proprietor, all the partners of a firm or all the officers of a foreign company ... does not or do
-- not reside in Singapore", it "must appoint ... at least one authorised representative".
-- s 11(14): "(a) a corporation resides outside Singapore if the corporation is incorporated or formed outside Singapore; and (b) an
-- individual resides outside Singapore if the individual's residential address is outside Singapore."
-- s 11(2): the representative must be "(a) a natural person; (b) at least 18 years of age; (c) otherwise of full legal capacity;
-- and (d) ordinarily resident in Singapore."

DECLARE `Partner` HAS
    `is a corporation`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `was incorporated or formed in Singapore`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a residential address in Singapore`    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A `Partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does the partner reside outside Singapore` IF
    IF `p`'s `is a corporation`
    THEN NOT `p`'s `was incorporated or formed in Singapore`
    ELSE NOT `p`'s `has a residential address in Singapore`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I carry on business`
      `my residential address is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partners` IS A LIST OF `Partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I appoint an authorised representative` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `as an individual proprietor` THEN NOT `my residential address is in Singapore`
    WHEN `as a partner of a firm` THEN all (GIVEN `p` YIELD `does the partner reside outside Singapore` `p`) `the partners`

GIVEN `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `has full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this person be my authorised representative` IF
        `is a natural person`
    AND `age in years` AT LEAST 18
    AND `has full legal capacity`
    AND `is ordinarily resident in Singapore`

-- s 11(3): if not resident at registration, appoint "at the time ... registered" or, if business starts later, "not later than the
-- date on which [it] commences to carry on business". s 11(4): ceasing to reside after registration: "within 30 days" (for a firm,
-- after the last resident partner ceases). s 11(11): the sole representative ceases or ceases to be qualified: "within 30 days".
-- The answer is days after the event named; 0 means on the day of the event itself.

DECLARE `Why I need a representative` IS ONE OF
    `I was not resident when I registered`
    `I stopped residing in Singapore after registering`
    `the last partner resident in Singapore stopped residing here`
    `my sole authorised representative ceased or stopped qualifying`

GIVEN `why` IS A `Why I need a representative`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to appoint an authorised representative` IS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `I was not resident when I registered` THEN 0
    -- on registration, or on the later day business commences
    WHEN `I stopped residing in Singapore after registering` THEN 30
    WHEN `the last partner resident in Singapore stopped residing here` THEN 30
    WHEN `my sole authorised representative ceased or stopped qualifying` THEN 30

§§ `ss 11(7), 11(9), 19, 20, 22 -- the notices I must lodge, and by when`

-- s 11(7): notice of the appointment and of the representative's consent "within 14 days after the date of appointment".
-- s 11(9): notice that the representative has ceased, or ceased to be qualified, "within 14 days after that event".
-- s 19(1): a registered individual proprietor, partner of a registered firm, or authorised representative "must lodge ... a notice
-- of the individual's new residential address within 14 days after the date of change"; (2) a report under s 10 of the National
-- Registration Act 1965 "is to be taken" as informing the Registrar.
-- s 20(1): a change in registered particulars, "within 14 days after the change, or such further period as the Registrar may on
-- application allow"; (2) not a change of residential address, nor of the registered business name (which goes by s 18).
-- s 20(3): a person who ceases to be a partner, and the continuing partners, "within 14 days after the cessation".
-- s 22(1): a registered person who stops carrying on business under a registered name, "within 14 days after so stopping".
-- NOTHING: no notice under these sections is needed.

DECLARE `What happened` IS ONE OF
    `I appointed an authorised representative`
    `my authorised representative ceased or stopped qualifying`
    `I changed my residential address`
    `another registered particular changed`
    `I want to change my registered business name`
    `I ceased to be a partner of a registered firm`
    `I stopped carrying on business under my registered name`

GIVEN `what` IS A `What happened`
      `I reported the new address under the National Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `further days the Registrar allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to lodge notice` IS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `I appointed an authorised representative` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `my authorised representative ceased or stopped qualifying` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `I changed my residential address` THEN
        IF `I reported the new address under the National Registration Act` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST 14
    WHEN `another registered particular changed` THEN JUST (14 PLUS `further days the Registrar allowed`)
    WHEN `I want to change my registered business name` THEN NOTHING
    -- an application under s 18, not a notice
    WHEN `I ceased to be a partner of a registered firm` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `I stopped carrying on business under my registered name` THEN JUST 14

-- s 22(4): on receipt of the notice "the registration of the person and the person's business name ... ceases".
-- The s 22(1) duty as a regulative rule, counted in days from the day I stopped.
DECLARE `Actor` IS ONE OF `the registered person`
DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF `lodge notice that I have stopped carrying on business under the name`

`my duty to give notice that I stopped` MEANS
    PARTY `the registered person`
    MUST `lodge notice that I have stopped carrying on business under the name`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST BREACH BY `the registered person`

§§ `ss 14(4), 24 -- after expiry, and restoring a registration`

-- s 14(4): "A person and the person's business name continue to be registered after the registration ... has expired unless the
-- registration is cancelled."
GIVEN `it has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still registered after my registration expired` IF NOT `it has been cancelled`

-- s 24(1): a person whose registration "has been cancelled under section 12(2), 14 or 23, or ... has ceased under section 22, may
-- lodge an application ... to restore". (2) "within 12 months after the date on which the registration was cancelled or had
-- ceased; or (b) within such longer time as the Registrar may in special circumstances allow."
-- A cancellation under s 12(1) or s 17(8) is not in the list, so restoration is not available for it.

DECLARE `How my registration ended` IS ONE OF
    `cancelled under section 12(1)`
    -- unlawful purpose, national security, a Charities Act conviction, or no authorised representative
    `cancelled after the CPF Board notified unpaid contributions`
    -- s 12(2)
    `cancelled for failure to renew`
    -- s 14
    `cancelled for not obeying a direction to change my name`
    -- s 17(8)
    `cancelled because I was not carrying on business`
    -- s 23
    `ceased when I gave notice that I stopped`
    -- s 22

GIVEN `how ended` IS A `How my registration ended`
      `whole months since it ended` IS A NUMBER
      `the Registrar allows longer for special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to restore my registration` IF
        `the kind is restorable`
    AND (   `whole months since it ended` LESS THAN 12
         OR `the Registrar allows longer for special circumstances`)
    WHERE
        `the kind is restorable` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how ended`
            WHEN `cancelled after the CPF Board notified unpaid contributions` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `cancelled for failure to renew` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `cancelled because I was not carrying on business` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `ceased when I gave notice that I stopped` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 35, 36 -- am I committing an offence by trading?`

-- s 35(1)(a): any person "being a person required to be registered" who (i) "carries on business in Singapore without being
-- registered"; (ii) under a business name "different from the person's registered business name"; or (iii) after the registration
-- "has been cancelled" or "has ceased".
-- s 35(2): "It is not an offence ... if the person is not required to be registered in respect of the business name under section 4."
-- s 24(5): restoration does not prevent prosecution under s 35(1)(a).

DECLARE `My registration` IS ONE OF
    `never registered`
    `registered under the name I trade under`
    `registered under a different name`
    `registration cancelled`
    `registration ceased`

GIVEN `my business` IS A `My business`, `registration` IS A `My registration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence by trading` IF
        `Must I register` `my business`
    AND NOT `registration` EQUALS `registered under the name I trade under`

-- s 36: if "proof is given that a business name has been displayed in any premises" and evidence from which the court may infer it
-- refers to a business carried on there, the person carrying on the business "is, in the absence of proof to the contrary,
-- presumed to be carrying on the business under that business name."
GIVEN `the name was displayed at my premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court may infer it refers to my business there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to trade under the displayed name` IF
        `the name was displayed at my premises`
    AND `the court may infer it refers to my business there`
    AND NOT `I prove the contrary`

-- s 34(1): an undischarged bankrupt (Singapore or foreign adjudication) who (a) "is required to be registered and who carries on any
-- business in Singapore", or (b) "takes part in or is concerned in the management of any business carried on by any person required
-- to be registered", "without the permission of the General Division of the High Court or the written permission of the Official
-- Assignee", commits an offence.
GIVEN `I am an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I must register and carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I take part in managing a business of someone who must register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have the High Court's or the Official Assignee's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I committing an offence as an undischarged bankrupt` IF
        `I am an undischarged bankrupt`
    AND (   `I must register and carry on business in Singapore`
         OR `I take part in managing a business of someone who must register`)
    AND NOT `I have the High Court's or the Official Assignee's written permission`

§§ `ss 11(12), 22(3), 34, 35, 37 -- what I can be fined, and what composition can cost`

-- s 35(1): $10,000 fine or 2 years or both. s 35(3) (ss 19(1), 20(1), 20(3)): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 22(3) (s 22(1)): fine not exceeding $5,000. s 11(12) (s 11(1), (7), (9)): fine not exceeding $1,000.
-- s 34(1): $10,000 or 2 years or both.
-- s 37(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for a sum "not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half
-- of the amount of the maximum fine" and (b) "$5,000". No regulations were deposited; whether an offence is prescribed is asked.

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `trading when I must be registered and am not`
    `failing without lawful excuse to obey a Registrar's summons`
    `knowingly giving the Registrar false information`
    `not notifying a new address or changed particulars or leaving a firm`
    `not notifying that I stopped business`
    `not appointing or not notifying an authorised representative`
    `carrying on business as an undischarged bankrupt without permission`

DECLARE `Maximum punishment` HAS
    `fine in dollars`   IS A NUMBER
    `prison in months`  IS A NUMBER
    -- 0: no imprisonment

GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished with` IS
    CONSIDER `offence`
    --                                                                                       fine,   prison
    WHEN `trading when I must be registered and am not`                         THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 10000, 24
    WHEN `failing without lawful excuse to obey a Registrar's summons`          THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 10000, 24
    WHEN `knowingly giving the Registrar false information`                     THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 10000, 24
    WHEN `not notifying a new address or changed particulars or leaving a firm` THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 5000,  12
    WHEN `not notifying that I stopped business`                                THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 5000,  0
    WHEN `not appointing or not notifying an authorised representative`        THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 1000,  0
    WHEN `carrying on business as an undischarged bankrupt without permission`  THEN `Maximum punishment` OF 10000, 24

GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined` IS
    (`What is the most I can be punished with` `offence`)'s `fine in dollars`

GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` IS
    (`What is the most I can be punished with` `offence`)'s `prison in months`

GIVEN `offence` IS AN `Offence`, `it is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound` IS
    IF `it is prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN JUST (BRANCH IF `half the fine` LESS THAN 5000 THEN `half the fine`
                      OTHERWISE 5000)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `half the fine` MEANS `What is the most I can be fined` `offence` DIVIDED BY 2
